// endpoint_update_persistent_wifi_mode.proto — UpdatePersistentWifiMode: turn
// the host machine's persistent wifi mode (lid-closed operation) on, off, or
// over. HOST MACHINE section. Daemon-scoped: nothing here names a workspace,
// and Emacs calls it over its one daemon-level connection.
//
// THE CHANGE RUNS IN THIS ORDER, and the order is the contract:
//   1. the hotspot — joined when turning on, left when turning off — FIRST, so
//      the network is settled before anything else;
//   2. the power settings — sleep disabled (on) or enabled (off), together
//      with network-over-sleep and wake-on-network — the one step that
//      decides whether the change happened at all;
//   3. the energy mode — low power (on) or high power (off) — once the
//      machine is known to stay awake, so a lid-closed machine draws as
//      little as it can and an open one runs at full speed again;
//   4. the display — LAST, and only where the change moves it: put to sleep
//      when turning on with the lid closed, woken when turning off with the
//      display asleep for the quiet state (UpdatePersistentWifiModeDisplay).
// A failed hotspot, energy mode or display step never stops the change:
// staying awake on whatever network is present is still the outcome asked
// for, so those three steps report how they went inside the SUCCESS, and only
// a refused power step is a failure.

